-- Seed: the Israeli holiday calendar, 2024-2030, from Hebcal.
--
-- Fetched once from https://www.hebcal.com/hebcal with maj=on&min=on&mod=on and
-- i=on (the Israel schedule -- without it Shavuot comes back as two days and every
-- festival is shifted for the diaspora). 413 rows, category=holiday only.
--
-- Fetched once and committed rather than fetched at run time: a seed that depends
-- on a live API is not reproducible, and the day the API changes shape or goes down
-- the database stops being restorable.
--
-- EVERY ROW CARRIES source='hebcal'. This is not a number invented here -- it is a
-- calendar from a verifiable source, and each row says so, which is exactly what
-- the tax-threshold table cannot say and why that one is still empty.
--
-- is_non_working DEFAULTS FROM yomtov, and yomtov is a halachic fact: it marks the
-- seven days a year on which work is forbidden (Rosh Hashana I-II, Yom Kippur,
-- Sukkot I, Shmini Atzeret, Pesach I and VII, Shavuot). That default is right for
-- those seven and wrong for at least one other day -- see the correction at the
-- bottom, which is the human layer doing its job on its first day.
--
-- Shabbat is deliberately absent: every Saturday is non-working and that is
-- arithmetic, not data.
--
-- Idempotent: on conflict do nothing. That is also what protects a human decision
-- from a re-run -- an existing row is never touched, so a hand-set is_non_working
-- survives.
--
-- Source of truth: docs/entities/holidays.md


on conflict (holiday_date, name) do nothing;

-- ── the human layer, correcting the machine on its first day ──
--
-- Hebcal returns Yom HaAtzma'ut with yomtov=false, because yomtov is a halachic
-- category and Independence Day is not one. It is nonetheless a statutory day of
-- rest in Israel: offices are closed and a filing deadline cannot land on it. The
-- default inherited from yomtov is therefore wrong for exactly this day.
--
-- Flagged as source='manual' rather than quietly patched into the hebcal rows, so
-- that the row says out loud that a person decided this and the import must not
-- touch it. This is the two-layer design working the day it was built.
--
-- ⚠️ FOR YITZHAK TO CONFIRM: this is the only correction applied. Erev chag (half
-- working days), chol hamoed, fasts and Purim are all left as working days. Whether
-- a deadline actually shifts off any of those is an administrative question about
-- how the authority behaves, not a fact anyone can look up -- so nothing was
-- guessed.
update holidays
   set is_non_working = true,
       source         = 'manual',
       notes          = 'שבתון על פי חוק. Hebcal מסמן yomtov=false כי זו קטגוריה הלכתית, ויום העצמאות אינו יום טוב — אבל המשרדים סגורים ומועד הגשה אינו יכול לחול בו.'
 where name_en like 'Yom HaAtzma%'
   and source = 'hebcal';
